{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence iteratively using a sliding window.\n    The sequence is defined by base cases and a sum of the previous four terms.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # For n > 3, use a sliding window [fib4(k-4), fib4(k-3), fib4(k-2), fib4(k-1)]\n    # Initial window stores fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n    fib_values = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = sum(fib_values)\n        # Slide the window: remove the oldest value and add the new one\n        fib_values.pop(0)\n        fib_values.append(next_fib)\n\n    return fib_values[3]"}
